ckedAt":1789073350752},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is mostly a Xiaohongshu research guide, but it tells users to clone, install, and run mutable third-party scraper code without pinning or integrity checks.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Running a scraper and packet-capture/reverse-engineering workflow can expose account sessions, local environment data, and scraped user content; the skill gives some compliance warnings but not enough containment guidance for executing third-party code.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill package itself contains only Markdown and package metadata, with no embedded executable scripts or install hooks.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"SKILL.md includes direct commands to clone a third-party GitHub scraper, install its requirements, and run it; the instructions do not pin a reviewed commit, verify dependencies, or recommend isolation before executing remote code.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, background workers, scheduled tasks, or memory modification were found in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, Xiaohongshu trend and note analysis, coherently matches the recommended manual browsing, scraping, and third-party tooling workflows.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review the external scraper before running it, pin it to a trusted commit, use a fresh virtual environment or container, avoid exposing browser profiles or credentials, and confirm that any scraping or packet capture complies with Xiaohongshu rules and applicable privacy obligations.","findings":"[T03] expected: Use of a Xiaohongshu scraper is purpose-aligned, but the exact documented workflow executes mutable third-party code and remotely selected Python dependencies without verification.\n[SQP-2] expected: Scraping and third-party tooling are expected for this platform analysis use case; SKILL.md includes account-risk and personal-research warnings, but README.md is thinner and neither file covers dependency integrity or isolation adequately.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-language content is coherent for a Xiaohongshu-specific skill and does not indicate malicious behavior; it is mainly a localization and disclosure issue.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789073350752}}}}}